  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-02-23T16:06:27.827Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "There are so many people named “fluffy” (for example) and only so many ways to make the username unique. Most of them involve annoying Unicode hacks that are only inconsistently allowed and cause other problems, and usually what people see is what they call others which also doesn’t work well for people with very common names. Wouldn’t it be great if we had a display name that’s separate from our username, similar to Discord?\n\nNote that on Discord people can still see the underlying username through a number of means and of course the VRChat version would ideally do that as well, and the name change cooldown limits would also still be in effect.",
